# Prettier ignores.
#
# This deliberately MIRRORS the ignore list in eslint.config.mjs, for the same
# reasons documented there. Read that file before adding or removing a line.

# Build output and generated files.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
next-env.d.ts
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Git worktrees. Each one is a FULL second checkout of this repo, so a naive
# `prettier --write .` would reformat every source file once per worktree,
# against a different branch's code. Prettier does not read .gitignore.
.claude/worktrees/

# Feature-pipeline reference material: Claude Design artboards and their
# compiled `_ds_bundle.js`. Copied in verbatim to be READ, not run or edited.
work/

# Vendored agent-skill tooling: largely bundled/minified browser scripts.
.agents/

# SQL migrations — EXCLUDED ON PURPOSE, not by oversight.
#
# Two independent reasons, either sufficient:
#
#   1. An applied migration is an immutable historical record. Reformatting one
#      creates a diff against a file that by definition must never change, and
#      this repo's migrations folder already runs ~100 behind the live database.
#   2. 55 of 125 migrations carry dollar-quoted bodies ($$ ... $$) and 31 use
#      CREATE POLICY / plpgsql / SECURITY DEFINER. That is exactly the syntax
#      SQL formatters mangle — a reformat here can produce SQL that no longer
#      means what it meant.
#
# Write migrations by hand. `supabase/functions/` (Deno TypeScript) IS
# formatted — it is excluded from ESLint over import resolution, which is a
# linting concern, not a formatting one.
supabase/migrations/

# Design tokens — EXCLUDED so hex stays uppercase.
#
# Prettier lowercases hex colours and offers no option to stop it. This file is
# a transcription of the Advantage Design System, and CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md,
# DESIGN.md and .skills/advantage-analytics-design/SKILL.md all quote its
# values in uppercase (#3B82F6, #5DB955, #E51837, ...). Lowercasing them here
# would silently break `grep` between the docs and the code.
#
# Only colors.css is excluded, not globals.css. Every documented token appears
# in BOTH, and more often here (#3B82F6 x5 vs x3), so this file alone preserves
# the grep target — while globals.css, a 651-line stylesheet with 81 real rules,
# stays formatted for everything added to it later. The other four
# design-system files touch no hex at all and are formatted normally.
src/styles/design-system/colors.css

# GENERATED FILES — never let a second tool format these.
#
# MAP.md is written by scripts/generate-map.mjs, and tests/generate-map.spec.ts
# asserts the committed file is byte-for-byte what the generator produces
# (`expect(after).toBe(before)`). Prettier rewrites *emphasis* as _emphasis_ and
# pads markdown tables, so formatting it makes `npm test` fail AND puts the two
# tools in an endless fight: format -> regenerate -> format -> ...
#
# Any future generated file belongs here for the same reason.
MAP.md

# supabase/email-templates/*.html are written by scripts/build_email_templates.py.
# Two reasons beyond "it is generated": the next generator run would clobber any
# formatting anyway, and src/lib/services/email/shell.ts is a HAND-COPY of this
# markup — docs/email-system.md requires the two stay in step, which a one-sided
# reformat silently breaks.
supabase/email-templates/

# Lockfile: 385 KB of generated JSON. Reformatting it would be a catastrophic
# diff and npm rewrites it anyway.
package-lock.json

# Derived stroke data, regenerated by scripts/splitstep_json_to_csv.py.
analysis/data/

# Non-JS languages handled by their own formatters in .githooks/format-file.sh
# (shell -> shfmt, Python -> black). Listed so `prettier --write .` does not
# try and fail on them.
*.sql
*.sh
*.py
*.toml
